  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "urn:npc-team:schema:finding-schema:6",
  "title": "NPC-team canonical pentest finding",
  "description": "Canonical machine-readable form of a pentest finding. This is the schema the skill instructions refer to as 'skills/autonomous-pentester/shared/finding_schema.json' (see e.g. skills/NPC-PEN-Cipher-0178/SKILL.md:42) and as the 'canonical finding_schema format' that findings must be written in (skills/NPC-PEN-Cipher-0178/SKILL.md:22). It is not an invention: the required field set is exactly the finding object emitted by the package's own producers in all 22 of their scripts (skills/NPC-PEN-*/scripts/*.py and skills/NPC-MOB-Solace-0019/scripts/mobile_auditor.py, function build_finding), which agree 22/22 on all 18 required names. The optional fields carry the evidence contract of references/domains/03-pentest.md section 5 and the evidence five-tuple of references/evidence-and-gates.md section 1. Result-envelope status (pass/fail/error/unsupported/skipped/not_executed) is governed by references/result-status-contract.md and belongs to the result envelope, not to this finding object.",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
